<title>USA: CME pork belly futures move sharply higher.</title>
<headline>CME pork belly futures move sharply higher.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME pork belly futures were sharply higher at mid-morning with gains largely the result of short covering after recent steep declines, traders said.</p>
<p>Much of the buying appeared to be from locals and commission houses.</p>
<p>CME July pork bellies closed at 76.900 cents per lb Friday versus 90.250 on June 4.</p>
<p>At 1036 CDT, pork bellies were up 2.550 to 0.800 cent with July up the most at 79.450 cents.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
